Eligible Users may fund their account through supported methods and may withdraw available Naira balances to supported Nigerian bank accounts, subject to applicable limits, verification, fraud controls and provider availability.

A deposit or withdrawal may be delayed, rejected, reversed or subjected to further review where:
a. information supplied is incorrect or incomplete;
b. the transaction exceeds an applicable limit;
c. further verification is required;
d. fraud or unauthorised activity is suspected;
e. a service provider rejects or reverses the transaction;
f. a legal or regulatory requirement prevents processing; or
g. technical or financial infrastructure necessary to complete the transaction is unavailable.

A transaction displayed as pending has not necessarily been finally settled.

Blockchain transactions may be irreversible.

You are responsible for verifying the supported asset, blockchain network, deposit address, memo or tag where applicable, and other transaction information before transmitting a digital asset.

NePay may not be able to recover assets sent:
a. using an unsupported blockchain network;
b. to an incorrect address;
c. without a required memo or tag;
d. in an unsupported digital asset; or
e. contrary to the transaction instructions presented to you.

NePay does not guarantee recovery of an erroneous blockchain transaction.

Digital asset deposits may require sufficient blockchain confirmations before settlement. Confirmation times may be affected by network congestion, protocol conditions and other matters outside Circle Technology's reasonable control.

You must not use NePay to:
a. commit fraud, money laundering, terrorist financing or any unlawful activity;
b. transact with unlawfully obtained funds, digital assets or gift cards;
c. impersonate another person;
d. circumvent transaction, KYC or security limits;
e. create accounts using false or misleading information;
f. manipulate rewards or referral programmes;
g. interfere with the security or operation of the Services;
h. introduce malicious code;
i. use automated means to access the Services without authorisation;
j. reverse engineer or attempt to extract proprietary source code except to the limited extent such restriction is prohibited by applicable law; or
k. use the Services in any manner prohibited by applicable law.

NePay may place a hold on a transaction or restrict, suspend or limit an account where reasonably necessary to:
a. investigate suspected fraud or unauthorised activity;
b. satisfy KYC, AML, sanctions or other compliance requirements;
c. respond to a lawful request or order;
d. protect the User, NePay or another person from reasonably suspected harm;
e. investigate a disputed transaction;
f. address a security incident;
g. enforce these Terms; or
h. comply with requirements imposed by an underlying service provider where reasonably applicable to the Services.

Where legally and operationally permissible, restrictions will be reviewed and removed when the underlying reason has been resolved.

Account restriction does not transfer ownership of a User's legitimate funds to Circle Technology.
